  "details": "Idea provided by : Ralph MacSavage\nEncrypt the locally cached data you store on people's PC's & work towards fixing problems like asset ripping instead of feigning solutions with thoughtless actions that only serve to ostracize those you refuse to cater towards, especially when your community works towards filling those gaps for them when you don't.\nsetting optimization requirements with good documentation for New comers & limiters on what people can throw at the Network by identifying & isolating abusive users would do wonders in helping your game run more efficiently for more people & start in a good direction to combat crashers.\n(that of course takes careful balancing between abusive users & those who just have bad connections & no alternative available options, so that'd probably get scuffed as well.)",
